const title = "Rooms & Exits Chapter 2 Level 22 Walkthrough: Print Shop";
const description = "Rooms & Exits Chapter 2 Level 22 walkthrough for the Print Shop: the four jersey numbers behind the till code 133951, the CD in the cash drawer, the ink cartridge that unfreezes the big printer, the six-segment wheel whose missing number is 54, and the printed sheet that feeds the exit door — whose keypad takes a different one of its six numbers in every playthrough.";

const faq = [
  {
    q: "What is the code for the cash register in Rooms & Exits Chapter 2 Level 22?",
    a: "Type <b>133951</b> on the register's touchscreen. The digits are the four jersey numbers hanging around the shop — HARRY <b>3</b>, NERO <b>13</b>, JACOB <b>9</b>, DANNY <b>51</b> — read as 13 · 3 · 9 · 51. Our two full recordings of the current build both end with <b>133951</b> on the register display, and both open the cash drawer and hand over the CD. The wall's left-to-right order, <b>313951</b>, is typed on screen at 3:00 in our long run and rejected — the field clears and the drawer stays shut — so do not just copy the jerseys in the order they hang.",
  },
  {
    q: "Where does the CD come from?",
    a: "The cash drawer under the register. Once <b>133951</b> is accepted the drawer slides open and holds three things: a stack of small clear bags on the left, a small red object in the middle and a single iridescent <b>CD</b> on the right. The CD is the only one you need; tap it and it goes into the bag as <b>CD</b>.",
  },
  {
    q: "What do I do with the CD?",
    a: "Use it on the desktop computer, not the printer. The PC sits on the L-shaped counter under the yellow DANNY 51 jersey, with a tower beside the monitor. Put the CD in the tower and the monitor changes to a printer icon with a red cross and the line <b>Nothing can be printed before the printer is fixed!</b> That message is the level telling you the print job exists but the hardware is not ready yet.",
  },
  {
    q: "Why does the big printer say it is missing something?",
    a: "Because it has no ink. Tap the floor-standing printer on the right-hand wall and it reports <b>The printer is missing something in order to work!</b> Select an <b>Ink cartridge</b> in the inventory, press <b>Use</b>, and tap the printer: the cartridge goes in, the panel lights up with its colour rows and the print job unlocks. The cartridge itself is a fat orange block with a small code printed on the side; the first one in our run comes out of the low cabinet under the left-hand mug and plate display at 1:39.",
  },
  {
    q: "What is the answer to the six-segment wheel?",
    a: "<b>54</b>. The wheel on the computer monitor carries 8, 13, 18, 24, 39 and one question mark, and the numbers sit in opposite pairs that triple: <b>8 × 3 = 24</b> and <b>13 × 3 = 39</b>, so <b>18 × 3 = 54</b>. Type 54 on the monitor's two-row keypad (1 2 3 4 5 over 6 7 8 9 0) and press <b>PRINT</b> — the field does not submit itself. Both of our full recordings type 54 and both get <b>PRINTING</b> on the copier within seconds.",
  },
  {
    q: "How do I get the Printed picture?",
    a: "Solve the wheel, press PRINT, then wait for the floor printer to finish. Its panel reads <b>PRINTING</b> and a sheet lands on the output tray; collect it and the item is in your bag as <b>Printed picture</b> — a six-slice colour wheel with 8, 13, 18, 24, 39 and 54 printed into the slices. Do not skip the pickup: the exit keypad stays dead until the sheet is in your inventory, and the sheet itself is the door's code list.",
  },
  {
    q: "What is the door code in the Print Shop?",
    a: "There is no single door code. The exit keypad wants one of the six numbers printed on the <b>Printed picture</b> — 8, 13, 18, 24, 39 or 54 — and which one it accepts changes between playthroughs: our three recordings opened on <b>8</b>, <b>18</b> and <b>24</b>, and 8 was refused outright in the run that opened on 24. Type them one at a time, clearing with the X key between attempts, until the door swings. It is a single number each time, not the six run together, and the keypad does nothing at all until the sheet is in your bag.",
  },
  {
    q: "Is there a key in Level 22?",
    a: "There is a keyhole — an oval lock plate under the exit keypad — but we never see a key in it or a key being picked up in any of the three recordings, and every run finishes on the keypad code alone. So no, you do not need to hunt for a key to leave the Print Shop. If a key exists in this level, it is not what opens this door.",
  },
  {
    q: "How long does the Print Shop take, and what does it pay?",
    a: "Two of our three recordings end on the same results screen: <b>+50 coins</b> under Reward and <b>9:52</b> on the results clock in the full run. The third, a 2:55 run of the same shop, shows a different panel — a +5 efficiency figure and no coin reward — which we treat as a build difference rather than a level rule. Nothing is timed and there is no fail state — the clock is scoring, not pressure — so the only things that really cost you minutes are typing the till code in the wrong order and working through six door candidates at the end.",
  },
  {
    q: "What difficulty is Chapter 2 Level 22?",
    a: "The level-select card lists <b>Level 22: Print Shop</b> as <b>Very Hard</b>, inside the Chapter 2 block <i>No Honor Among Thieves</i>. That rating is about the number of separate locks rather than any one hard puzzle: a till code, a CD, a cartridge, a wheel and a door, and every one of them gates the next.",
  },
];

const faqJsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  mainEntity: faq.map((f) => ({
    "@type": "Question",
    name: f.q,
    acceptedAnswer: { "@type": "Answer", text: f.a.replace(/<[^>]+>/g, "") },
  })),
};
