<body>
  <GameNav />
  <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> &gt; <a href="/rooms-and-exits/">Rooms &amp; Exits</a> &gt; <a href="/rooms-and-exits/">Chapter 2</a> &gt; Level 22</nav>

  <main class="seo-section">
    <h1>Rooms &amp; Exits Chapter 2 Level 22 Walkthrough: Print Shop</h1>

    <div class="disclaimer">Unofficial fan-made guide. Not affiliated with Webelinx Games, the developer of Rooms &amp; Exits: Escape Room Games.</div>

    <div class="verify-note">Built from three independent recordings of this room: a 10:40 full run extracted at one frame per second, a 2:55 quick run of the same shop used as a second read, and a 4:44 run used as a third opinion and as a tie-breaker. Every number this page prints — <b>133951</b> on the till, <b>54</b> on the wheel, the four jersey numbers, the six numbers on the printed sheet, <b>+50</b> and <b>9:52</b> on the results panel — was read off the screen twice or more, and the till code was read from two different videos. The exit door is the one place the recordings disagree in a way that matters: each run typed a different number and each run opened on a different one, so the page gives you all six candidates and says so plainly instead of inventing a single code. On-screen text was read with optical character recognition on the raw frames and then checked by eye on magnified crops, not typed from memory, and every timestamp below points at the exact second of the embedded run.</div>

    <LevelSelector chapter={2} current={22} variant="jump" label="Chapter 2 · No Honor Among Thieves" />

    <div class="answer-box">
      <span class="label">Quick answer</span>
      <p>Print Shop is a chain of locks, and the numbers you need are <b>133951</b> for the till, <b>54</b> for the printing wheel, and then one of the six numbers on the sheet you print for the door. The exit is the grey-framed glass door on the back wall; its keypad refuses some of those numbers and accepts one, and it is not the same one every time — our three runs opened on <b>8</b>, <b>18</b> and <b>24</b>, so work through 8 · 13 · 18 · 24 · 39 · 54 until the door swings. Finish worth <b>+50 coins</b>.</p>
      <ol>
        <li>Read the four jerseys: HARRY <b>3</b>, NERO <b>13</b>, JACOB <b>9</b>, DANNY <b>51</b>.</li>
        <li>Type the till code <b>133951</b> → cash drawer opens → take the <b>CD</b>.</li>
        <li>Use the <b>CD</b> on the desktop tower beside the monitor (this produces <i>Nothing can be printed before the printer is fixed!</i> in one recording; our long run skips it).</li>
        <li>Take an <b>Ink cartridge</b> (the first sits in the low cabinet under the left-hand mug display at 1:39) and use it on the big floor printer → <i>The printer is missing something in order to work!</i> clears.</li>
        <li>On the monitor, solve the wheel: 8 · 13 · 18 · 24 · 39 · ? triple in opposite pairs → type <b>54</b> → <b>PRINT</b>.</li>
        <li>Wait for <b>PRINTING</b>, then take the <b>Printed picture</b> from the bag.</li>
        <li>Tap the keypad on the glass door and type the numbers from the printed sheet until one is accepted — 8, 18 and 24 each worked in one of our runs → <b>+50 coins</b>.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="video-wrap">
            <div class="yt-facade" data-yt="CoU_2oFwxbI" data-title="Rooms &amp;amp; Exits Chapter 2 Level 22 Print Shop walkthrough"
           role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Play video: Rooms &amp;amp; Exits Chapter 2 Level 22 Print Shop walkthrough">
        <img src="https://i.ytimg.com/vi/CoU_2oFwxbI/maxresdefault.jpg"
             alt="Rooms &amp;amp; Exits Chapter 2 Level 22 Print Shop walkthrough" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1280" height="720"
             onerror="this.onerror=null;this.src='https://i.ytimg.com/vi/CoU_2oFwxbI/hqdefault.jpg'">
      </div>
    </div>

    <img class="hero" src="/rooms-and-exits/c2l22-hero-print-shop.jpg" alt="Rooms and Exits Chapter 2 Level 22 Print Shop: the shop floor with the mug and plate shelves on the left, the HARRY 3 and NERO 13 jerseys beside the glass door, the JACOB 9 jersey on the orange corner wall, the L-shaped counter with two monitors and a printer, and the DANNY 51 jersey above the big floor copier" width="1200" height="594" />

    <h2>What this level actually is<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <p>The Print Shop is level 22 on the map and the level-select card files it as <b>Very Hard</b> — which is the right rating for the wrong reason. There is no single brutal puzzle here. What makes it heavy is that the room is a production line: every lock feeds the next one, and most of them are gated behind an object you have to carry from one end of the shop to the other. You cannot shortcut the till to get to the wheel, and you cannot print anything until the printer has ink.</p>
    <p>The fiction is a custom merchandise shop: jerseys printed with names and numbers, mugs and plates with cartoon bears, caps, framed photos, cushions, and two clothing racks of blanks in the foreground. The shop is one open isometric floor with a fixed camera. Along the back wall, left to right: a shelving unit stacked with mugs on top and plates below, with a low wooden cabinet underneath; the blue <b>HARRY 3</b> jersey and the green <b>NERO 13</b> jersey; the grey-framed glass door you eventually leave through; an orange accent corner holding the red <b>JACOB 9</b> jersey, more mugs and caps; then the L-shaped service counter with two monitors, a desktop tower and a small white printer. On the right-hand wall hangs the yellow <b>DANNY 51</b> jersey, and under it the big floor-standing copier that does the actual print job. Front of house is the blue-lit sales counter with the till, and two clothing racks sitting in the middle of the floor.</p>
    <p>Everything you can see is either merchandise or a container, and the game is unusually strict about which is which. The mugs, plates, caps and cushions are scenery. The low cabinet, the till drawer, the desktop tower, the printer's cartridge bay and the shopping bag are the containers. Learning that split early saves you ten minutes of tapping crockery.</p>

    <h2>The map: what is where<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <p>If you only read one part of this page, read this table. Every object in the Print Shop that does something, and what it does.</p>
    <table class="item-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Object</th><th>Where</th><th>What it gives you</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Jerseys</td><td>Back wall and right wall</td><td>HARRY <b>3</b> (blue), NERO <b>13</b> (green), JACOB <b>9</b> (red), DANNY <b>51</b> (yellow). The digits for the till code.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Cash register</td><td>Front sales counter, centre</td><td>A touchscreen that opens a full QWERTY overlay. Takes the six-digit code and opens the drawer.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Cash drawer</td><td>Under the till</td><td>Clear bags, a small red object and the <b>CD</b>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Desktop computer</td><td>Counter, under DANNY 51</td><td>Monitor + tower. Takes the CD and shows the print-job warning — though one of our runs finishes without ever using the disc.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Big floor printer</td><td>Right wall, under DANNY 51</td><td>Takes the ink cartridge. Its panel shows <b>PRINTING</b> and feeds out the sheet.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Low cabinet</td><td>Under the left-hand mug display</td><td>First <b>Ink cartridge</b> of the level.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Mug and plate shelves</td><td>Back-left wall</td><td>Scenery. Six mugs with coloured handles, plates below. Nothing to solve here.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Caps and cushions</td><td>Orange corner unit</td><td>Scenery. The caps are the same three colours as some jerseys and mean nothing.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Paper bag</td><td>Floor in front of the counter</td><td>The shop's branded bag — a container, not a clue.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Clothing racks</td><td>Centre of the floor</td><td>Blank shirts, front and centre. Scenery.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Exit door</td><td>Back wall, beside NERO 13</td><td>Grey frame, blue glass, 3×3 keypad and a keyhole below it. The keypad takes one number from the printed sheet — the way out.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Wall clock</td><td>Orange corner</td><td>A photo-face clock. Decorative.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>Step by step<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <p>The timestamps below are the embedded run's clock, so you can scrub straight to the frame. The room's own timer sits about half a minute behind the video — the intro and the level card eat that — so do not be alarmed when the HUD and the video disagree by a few seconds.</p>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 1 · 0:01</span>
      <strong>The level card tells you the reward before you start</strong>
      The run opens on the level-select card: a hexagonal thumbnail of a shop with a printer and two shirts, the name <b>Print Shop</b>, a coin stack marked <b>+50</b>, and a green play button. The card is worth a second's attention for two reasons. First, it confirms the payout before you commit. Second, the level number under the icon and the <b>Very Hard</b> tag on the selected node are the game's own difficulty call — and it is honest about it, because this room has more moving parts than any of the three levels before it.
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CoU_2oFwxbI&t=1s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">0:01</a></div>
    </div>
    <InContentAd />

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 2 · 0:22</span>
      <strong>Read the room before you tap anything</strong>
      The opening wide shot is the only clean look you get at the whole floor. Fix it in your head in this order: shelves and low cabinet on the back-left, the two jerseys and the glass door along the back wall, the orange corner with a third jersey, the L-shaped counter with two monitors and a small printer, the yellow jersey and the big copier on the right wall, the till on the front counter, and the clothing racks in the middle of the floor. The one thing to notice is how much distance there is between the till and the printer: this level is designed around walking a CD and a cartridge across that floor, and the camera will make you do it more than once.
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CoU_2oFwxbI&t=22s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">0:22</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 3 · 0:50</span>
      <strong>The jerseys are the only code in the room — copy all four numbers</strong>
      The back wall carries two printed jerseys under spotlights: blue <b>HARRY 3</b> and green <b>NERO 13</b>. Pan right and the orange corner holds red <b>JACOB 9</b>; pan again and the right wall has yellow <b>DANNY 51</b>, in blue lettering that reads cleanly from across the shop. Four names, four numbers, and they are the only digits in the room that are not part of a screen or a label. Write all four down before you touch the till, because the entry field is far from the wall and you will not be able to read the jerseys while the code overlay is open.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/c2l22-jerseys-harry-nero-jacob.jpg" alt="The back wall of the Print Shop with the blue HARRY 3 jersey and the green NERO 13 jersey under spotlights, the mug and plate shelves on the left and the red JACOB 9 jersey on the orange corner wall to the right" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CoU_2oFwxbI&t=50s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">0:50</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 4 · 1:39</span>
      <strong>The first ink cartridge comes out of the low cabinet</strong>
      Under the mug and plate shelves on the back-left wall there is a low wooden cabinet. Open it and the game throws a fat orange ink cartridge up into the middle of the screen with the name <b>Ink cartridge</b> printed beneath it, and a burst of sparks behind the counter. The cartridge is squarish with a red top and a small code printed on its side; it is the first of the consumables this level runs on. It is also the single most skippable step in the room — a lot of players walk straight past it and only come back when the printer refuses to work twenty minutes later.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/c2l22-ink-cartridge.jpg" alt="An orange ink cartridge lifted out of a cabinet in the Print Shop, with the item label Ink cartridge underneath and two printed mugs visible in the cabinet behind" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CoU_2oFwxbI&t=99s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">1:39</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 5 · 1:52</span>
      <strong>The right wall: DANNY 51 and the machine that does the work</strong>
      The yellow <b>DANNY 51</b> jersey hangs above the biggest object in the room — a floor-standing copier with a document feeder on top, a light-blue control panel on its face and a paper tray at the bottom. This is the printer every warning in the level is talking about, and it is also the fourth jersey number, so the two things you need on this wall are in the same frame. Under the counter to its left sits the desktop computer that becomes important once you have the CD: monitor, tower, and a small white printer that is scenery.
